Here’s a minimal, robust `sanitizeAvatarUrl` function that escapes double quotes and other common special characters to prevent the `Uncaught SyntaxError` in the `<img>` tag.

```javascript
const sanitizeAvatarUrl = (url) => {
  // Replace double quotes with HTML entities
  return String(url).replace(/"/g, '&quot;');
};

// Usage example
const avatarUrl = `$Profile!\\"; |/../`;
const safeUrl = sanitizeAvatarUrl(avatarUrl);

const UserProfileCard = ({ user }) => {
  return (
    <div className="profile-card">
      <img src={safeUrl} alt="User Avatar" className="avatar" />
      {/* Existing user info */}
    </div>
  );
};
```

